{"id":895,"date":"2021-03-25T11:26:00","date_gmt":"2021-03-25T11:26:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=researcher&#038;p=895"},"modified":"2021-03-30T07:12:23","modified_gmt":"2021-03-30T07:12:23","slug":"maalvladedon-ganet-some","status":"publish","type":"researcher","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/researcher\/maalvladedon-ganet-some\/","title":{"rendered":"Maalvladedon Ganet Some"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim profile-banner bg-alt\" style=\"background-color:none\"><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Maalvladedon Ganet Some<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>PhD Student<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/WhatsApp-Image-2020-01-31-at-11.30.23-AM-1.jpg\"\/>\n\n\n<p>Maalvladedon Ganet Some is originally from Burkina Faso. He pursued his undergraduate studies at the University of Ghana where he graduated with a Bachelor of Science in Mathematics. Afterwards, he was admitted at the mathematics department of the same institution as a teaching assistant and subsequently as a graduate assistant.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Some\u2019s quest to deepen his understanding of mathematics and its applications led him to apply to AIMS Ghana and was awarded a Master of Science in Mathematical Sciences. Subsequently, he enrolled for a research master at the university of Ghana.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Currently, Some is a part-time tutor at AIMS Ghana and a PhD candidate in the stochastic and finance research group led by Prof. Olivier Menoukeu Pamen. His research interests include stochastic optimal control, backward stochastic differential equations (BSDEs) and risk measures.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Maalvladedon Ganet Some is originally from Burkina Faso. He pursued his undergraduate studies at the University of Ghana where he graduated with a Bachelor of Science in Mathematics. Afterwards, he was admitted at the mathematics department of the same institution as a teaching assistant and subsequently as a graduate assistant. Some\u2019s quest to deepen his<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":896,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-researchername":"Maalvladedon Ganet Some","profile-researchercountry":"","profile-researcherprogram":"PhD Student"},"tags":[],"researcher_types":[41],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/WhatsApp-Image-2020-01-31-at-11.30.23-AM-1.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/rose\/","display_name":"rose"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 5 years ago","modified":"Updated 5 years ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on March 25, 2021","modified":"Updated on March 30, 2021"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on March 25, 2021 11:26 am","modified":"Updated on March 30, 2021 7:12 am"},"featured_img_caption":"","tax_additional":{"post_tag":{"linked":[],"unlinked":[],"slug":"post_tag","name":"Tags"},"researcher_types":{"linked":["<a href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/researcher_type\/researcher\/\" class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">PhD Researcher<\/a>"],"unlinked":["<span class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">PhD Researcher<\/span>"],"slug":"researcher_types","name":"Researcher Type"}},"series_order":"","_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/researcher\/895"